123 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 92 0 R
/E (Food waste is a big problem in the Netherlands. In the Netherlands, approximately 127-161 kg of food per person is lost every year. Food waste is not only a waste but also bad for our climate. Before food reaches the supermarket, it's packaged and transported to your supermarket. This requires gasoline and use of fossil fuels. If you throw the food away, you waste the effort and materials used. Furthermore, food that is thrown away often rots. Rotting food releases methane gas, which contributes to the increased greenhouse effect. People often don't realize that throwing away food has a huge impact on the climate and they also don't realize that it's simply a waste of products)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
